      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "In questions, you'll use a shortcut. Turn each percentage into a fraction by dividing by a hundred, multiply each isotope's mass by its fraction, then add them up. For chlorine, the abundances are seventy-five point seven seven percent, and twenty-four point two three percent. Thirty-five times zero point seven five seven seven is twenty-six point five two. Thirty-seven times zero point two four two three is eight point nine seven. Add them, and you get thirty-five point four eight, about thirty-five point five. The periodic table says thirty-five point four five because it uses each isotope's exact mass, which is slightly less than thirty-five or thirty-seven.",
