      "pronunciationText": "Now the question in reverse. Suppose you know the relative atomic mass, and you want the abundances. In this question, silicon has a relative atomic mass of twenty-eight point two two, and we assume it has only two isotopes, silicon-twenty-eight and silicon-twenty-nine. Real silicon also has some silicon-thirty, so this is a simplified model. Let x be the fraction of silicon-twenty-eight. With only two isotopes, the fractions add to one, so silicon-twenty-nine is one minus x.",
